 ***************************************************              7831 1451
------ENDF-6 FORMAT                                               7831 1451
                                                                  7831 1451
                                                                  7831 1451
The description below is common to all 90-198 Pt isotope          7831 1451
evaluations.                                                      7831 1451
                                                                  7831 1451
Fast neutron evaluations for nine Pt isotopes were merged with    7831 1451
ENDF/B-VIII.0 resonance regions.                                  7831 1451
                                                                  7831 1451
The chain of isotopes has been evaluated in parallel in order to  7831 1451
make use of experimental data taken on the natural element,       7831 1451
which often are the most reliable source of information. In the   7831 1451
case ofPt the evaluation methodology was the same as the one      7831 1451
used for 181Ta. Dealing with a chain of several isotopes implies  7831 1451
that the consistency requirement must be imposed. We need to      7831 1451
ensure that the same model parameters are used when a given       7831 1451
isotope appears in different calculations. Technically, this      7831 1451
condition was imposed by defining the common input file           7831 1451
containing all input parameters except those pertinent to the     7831 1451
particular target , such as target A and Z, or coupled-channels   7831 1451
coupling scheme. This file was included while reading input       7831 1451
files for the individual isotopes. We used superfluid EGSM level  7831 1451
densities (except of 198Pt for which Gilbert-Cameron level        7831 1451
densities were used), and HRTW width fluctuation correction.      7831 1451
                                                                  7831 1451
The shape of the calculated capture cross sections is very        7831 1451
similar to the Koehler 2013 measurements.  We only scaled         7831 1451
down calculated cross sections with a single, energy-             7831 1451
independent factor per each isotope. These factors, which         7831 1451
multiply the original MLO1 gamma-strength, are closer to 1        7831 1451
than the default factors resulting from normalization to the      7831 1451
thermal gamma width.  Choosing to follow isotopic measurements    7831 1451
by Koehler we underestimate by about 5% the respectable           7831 1451
experiments on the natural platinum that were very                7831 1451
well reproduced with the default (thermal normalization)          7831 1451
calculations. There is a disagreement between these experiments   7831 1451
and those by Koehler. The LANSCE results will help to make a      7831 1451
final decision.                                                   7831 1451
                                                                  7831 1451
Elemental (n,2n) cross sections by Frehaut, corrected by a        7831 1451
factor of 1.078,  are  well reproduced by the new evaluation.     7831 1451
The  ENDF/B-VIII.0 is a bit lower but equally good. The two       7831 1451
evaluations differ mostly in the high energy tail where no        7831 1451
experimental data exist.                                          7831 1451
                                                                  7831 1451
In the case of (n,p) and (n,$\alpha$) reactions we followed       7831 1451
primarily data by Filatenkov. Ground-state cross sections agree   7831 1451
with ENDF/B-VIII.0 within uncertainties. No isomeric meta state   7831 1451
cross sections are given in the current ENDF/B-VIII.0             7831 1451
evaluations. Our (n,p) isomeric and ground state cross sections   7831 1451
reproduce measurements but at the price of modifying              7831 1451
particle-hole spin distribution in the preequilibrium emission    7831 1451
of protons.  The quite significant reduction is likely related    7831 1451
to the fact that Multistep Direct mechanism, that is here         7831 1451
simulated by the exciton model, favors low angular momentum       7831 1451
transfer populating states with the spin close to the ground      7831 1451
state.                                                            7831 1451
                                                                  7831 1451
The covariances were calculated used Kalman filter and include    7831 1451
cross-reaction correlations. Cross-isotope correlations were      7831 1451
not accounted for which implies that uncertainties are somewhat   7831 1451
overestimated since data on natural Pt were not considered in     7831 1451
uncertainty quantification.                                       7831 1451
                                                                  7831 1451
                                                                  7831 1451
 Nuclear reaction model code EMPIRE-3.2.3 Malta                   7831 1451
 (SVN rev.  5496; source rev.  5494)                              7831 1451
 by M.W.Herman et al [EMP,EMP-man].                               7831 1451
                                                                  7831 1451
 EMPIRE dimensions (dimension.h):                                 7831 1451
  NDNUC= 100  NDEXCLUS= 50  NDEX= 201  NDLW= 100                  7831 1451
  LEVCC= 40  NDLV= 40  NDBR= 40  NDMSCS= 4                        7831 1451
                                                                  7831 1451
 CROSS-SECTION EVALUATION PROCEDURE                               7831 1451
                                                                  7831 1451
 Adopted procedure is based on careful theoretical                7831 1451
 analysis utilizing available experimental data and               7831 1451
 nuclear reaction model calculations.                             7831 1451
                                                                  7831 1451
 This code integrates into a single system a number               7831 1451
 of important modules and features:                               7831 1451
                                                                  7831 1451
 - Spherical and deformed Optical Model including                 7831 1451
   coupled-channels code ECIS06 by J. Raynal                      7831 1451
 - Soft-rotator deformed Optical Model including                  7831 1451
   coupled-channels code OPTMAN by E.Soukhovitskii                7831 1451
   and coworkers                                                  7831 1451
 - Hauser-Feshbach statistical model including                    7831 1451
   width fluctuation correction, and the                          7831 1451
   optical model for fission with partial damping                 7831 1451
 - Quantum-mechanical MSD TUL model (codes ORION &                7831 1451
   TRISTAN by H.Lenske), and MSC NVWY model                       7831 1451
 - Exciton model with Iwamoto-Harada cluster                      7831 1451
   emission and Kalbach systematic angular distr.                 7831 1451
   (code PCROSS by R.Capote et al)                                7831 1451
 - Hybrid Monte Carlo preequilibrium model(M.Blann)               7831 1451
   (code DDHMS by M.Chadwick, mod. by B.V.Carlson)                7831 1451
 - Complete gamma-ray cascade after emission of                   7831 1451
   each particle, including realistic treatment of                7831 1451
   discrete transitions                                           7831 1451
 - Access to OM segment of the RIPL library [RIPL]                7831 1451
 - Built-in input parameter files, such as masses,                7831 1451
   level density, discrete levels, fission barriers               7831 1451
   and gamma strength functions based on the RIPL                 7831 1451
   library [RIPL]                                                 7831 1451
 - Automatic retrieval of experimental data from the              7831 1451
   EXFOR library                                                  7831 1451
 - ENDF-6 formatting (code EMPEND by A.Trkov)                     7831 1451
   coupled to graphical presentation capabilities                 7831 1451
   (code ZVView by V. Zerkin) through the chain of                7831 1451
   PrePro codes by D. Cullen                                      7831 1451
 - ENDF checking codes (CHECKR, FIZCON, PSYCHE)                   7831 1451
 - Highly automated fitting of optical model                      7831 1451
   parameters (by B.V. Carlson)                                   7831 1451
 - KALMAN code for fitting experimental data and                  7831 1451
 - generating covariances                                         7831 1451
 - Support for NJOY                                               7831 1451
                                                                  7831 1451
                                                                  7831 1451
