                                                                  7831 1451
  General methodology: The global approach considered in this     7831 1451
          work is presented in the following paper: Modern        7831 1451
          nuclear data evaluation with the TALYS code system,     7831 1451
          A.J. Koning and D. Rochman, Nuclear Data Sheets 113     7831 1451
          (2012) 2841.                                            7831 1451
                                                                  7831 1451
  MF2:  Resolved resonance range  (RRR)                           7831 1451
       The RRR was generated with TARES-1.31, compiled on         7831 1451
       12-10-2015 11:58:11 PM at Villingen  , Switzerland. The RRR7831 1451
       expands from 0 to 3.479356E+4 eV. A total of               7831 1451
       2 l-values are used and 456 resonances. The resonance      7831 1451
       formalism is multi-level Breit Wigner (MLBW).              7831 1451
       The ladder approach from the CALENDF code is used to       7831 1451
       generate statistical resonances in the unresolved          7831 1451
       resonance range. Therefore, the URR is translated into     7831 1451
       resolved resonance range. Explanations about the method    7831 1451
       can be found in the CALENDF manual: CEA-Report CEA-R-6277  7831 1451
       "CALENDF-2010: User manual" by J.C. Sublet, P. Ribon and   7831 1451
       M. Coste-Delcaux.                                          7831 1451
       The method of creating statistical resonances in the       7831 1451
       URR region is described in: "From average parameters to    7831 1451
       statistical resolved resonances", D. Rochman et al.,       7831 1451
       Annals of Nucl. Ene. 51 (2013) 60.                         7831 1451
       The s-wave average level spacing is 21.97 eV and           7831 1451
       the s-wave neutron strength is 0.00014 1e-4.               7831 1451
                                                                  7831 1451
  MF32: Covariance file for resonance parameters                  7831 1451
        The compact format is used to represent the covariance    7831 1451
        information on the resonance parameters. Uncertainties    7831 1451
        come from compilations, EXFOR or existing libraries and   7831 1451
        correlations between parameters are obtained following    7831 1451
        the method presented in NIM/A 589 (2008) 85.              7831 1451
